1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,200
This bridge tore itself apart in a 40-mile-an-hour wind.

2
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:10,350
The Tacoma Narrows Bridge opened in July 1940.

3
00:00:11,830 --> 00:00:16,300
Its deck was so thin and solid that steady wind made it twist,

4
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:20,950
harder and harder, until it ripped apart four months later.

5
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:26,700
Engineers learned that wind can shake a bridge to pieces.

6
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:31,900
That's why modern bridges are tested in wind tunnels first.
